<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bonaventure</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1221">1221</a>–<a href="/years/1274">1274</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Giovanni di Fidanza, Saint Bonaventure, Seraphic Doctor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bonaventure, born Giovanni di Fidanza at Civita di Bagnoregio in the Papal States, was an Italian Franciscan theologian and philosopher, Minister General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Order of Friars Minor</a>, cardinal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of Albano. He entered the Franciscan Order in 1243, studied at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-paris">University of Paris</a> and was received there as master in 1257. As the order's seventh Minister General he defended it against its critics and steered it on a moderate and intellectual course, and he wrote a life of Francis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assisi">Assisi</a>. His theology, set out in works such as The Mind's Road to God, sought to integrate faith and reason. He died suddenly at the Second Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> in 1274 and was canonised in 1482.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bonaventure.jpg" alt="Bonaventure" width="330" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Claude François · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:François,_Claude_(dit_Frère_Luc)_-_Saint_Bonaventure.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Bagnoregio, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=42.63,12.09&amp;year=1255" aria-label="Bagnoregio on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4843 649 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Bonaventure"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5293 919h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5293 919h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=42.63,12.09&amp;year=1255">What was here in 1255? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
